## Fix-round self-review

### State ordering and fixed-baseline objective

- Complete iterations remain investigator → author → local validation/discovery → critic → decision.
- `iterations/NNN` is durable before investigator authority; the complete three-role context plan is proved before the iteration is counted.
- Every accepted or failed finalized provider attempt enters exact accounting before its terminal outcome is normalized.
- Every candidate score remains relative to the original authenticated parity baseline; incumbent comparisons remain diagnostics only.
- A prospective improvement is context-proved and staged, then `decision.json` and `incumbent.diff` are made durable before live incumbent state or capability ownership changes.

### Critic-before-decision and safe failures

- All nonterminal closed validation failures, including the real cumulative/source oversize path and zero-discovery-trades path, retain the incumbent and receive critic review.
- Protocol, audit, identity, accounting, evidence, and evaluator-integrity failures remain terminal and cannot be rewritten as candidate feedback.
- The critic artifact remains durable before any `decision.json` or incumbent transition.

### Hidden boundary

- Provider capability closes before hidden evaluation and every later role call is rejected.
- Reservation, source, baseline, candidate, fold, independent reset, aggregate, and decision identities are authenticated before the holdout artifact.
- `holdout.json` is durable before hidden state can affect the result; write/sync failure leaves hidden state unset.
- A content-free validation-ledger outcome proof is required on success and on every caught hidden failure; no hidden content is placed in the ledger proof.

### Atomic artifacts and containment

- Immutable JSON artifacts remain canonical create-only files with file and parent-directory durability; accounting/incumbent snapshots retain atomic replacement.
- Round 1 component walking rejected pre-existing symlink/reparse metadata, but did not close a post-check/pre-mutation replacement race. This self-review statement was incomplete and is superseded by the handle-relative Fix Round 2 implementation and deterministic race test below.
- Numbered directories are explicitly created/synced and partial directories/artifacts are retained after terminal investigator/provider failures.
- Injected write and directory-sync failures prove no incumbent or hidden state advance.

### Capability disposal and terminal cleanup

- `CandidateWorkspace` remains inert; no authority is reconstructed from a root path.
- Prior incumbent disposal occurs only after the authoritative transition artifacts and live-state commit. A non-winning candidate is disposed only after its retain decision is durable.
- The common terminal path still disables provider use, closes the lease, attempts every candidate/worker cleanup, verifies inputs/source, replaces exact accounting, and attempts `summary.json` last.
- The separately reviewed Minor pre-registration ownership-transfer case was intentionally left unchanged because none of the blocking repairs required that path.

### Secrecy

- Provider-projectable inputs contain no hidden IDs, dates, metrics, outcomes, or reservation facts.
- Public result and exact artifact key-set tests exclude runtime capability paths, prompts, raw provider envelopes, credentials, headers, keys, and operator approval contents.
- Failed attempt artifacts contain only closed lifecycle facts and an optional accepted-payload digest; failed/uncertain records have `payload_sha256=null`.
- All committed fixtures are synthetic and all runtime artifacts/ledgers in tests use pytest temporary roots.

## Exact resource/effect statement

